ial report/secondary analysis of non-seizure outcomes in CDD; local PubMed metadata marks Clinical Trial Phase III/RCT. It does not provide extractable seizure efficacy outcomes for the plotted seizure columns.","status":"verified","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/38959712/"},{"label":"Sullivan2023","pmid":"36870093","proposed_action":"Keep.","rationale":"PubMed verifies a randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled phase 2 trial of oral ganaxolone versus placebo in PCDH19-clustering epilepsy, with ganaxolone maximum daily dose 63 mg/kg/day or 1800 mg/day and NCT03865732.","status":"verified","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/36870093/"},{"label":"Knight2022","pmid":"35429480","proposed_action":"Keep; disregard the deterministic title-only warning.","rationale":"PubMed verifies a randomized, placebo-controlled phase 3 trial of adjunctive ganaxolone versus placebo for CDD-associated refractory epilepsy. The title and abstract support the drug, seizure context, phase, randomization, and placebo control.","status":"verified","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/35429480/"},{"label":"Sperling2017","pmid":"28230252","proposed_action":"Keep.","rationale":"PubMed verifies a randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled phase 2 study of ganaxolone 1500 mg/day as add-on therapy in adults with uncontrolled partial-onset seizures.","status":"verified","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/28230252/"}],"source_updates":[{"current_value":"FDA Ztalmy approval/snapshot pages; FDA/DailyMed labeling","field":"evidence_sources","proposed_value":"FDA Ztalmy approval/snapshot pages; FDA prescribing information (Drugs@FDA/accessdata); PubMed RCT abstracts/metadata; ClinicalTrials.gov records for trial design where needed","reason":"Replace DailyMed with FDA label source and name PubMed/ClinicalTrials.gov support for RCT and outcome fields.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://www.fda.gov/drugs/drug-trials-snapshots/drug-trials-snapshots-ztalmy","https://